## To release a new version, edit the version in the two lines below and nothing else.
## |cRRGGBB...|r in Title and Author colours them in the in-game add-on list; the version
## is read back through that markup, so it can sit inside or outside the colour.
## The settings panel takes its version from ## Title; the name itself is fixed in Main.lua.
## Title: |cFF69B4PB’s ChatWindowCustomizer|r 1.3.0
## Author: |cFF69B4PinkBanther|r
## Description: Moves and resizes the chat window on the HUD, changes the size of the text in it, and can keep it on screen instead of fading out after 20 seconds -- in menus as well as on the HUD. Position is measured from whichever corner of the screen you choose, so the window grows away from that corner; width, height and message text size each have their own slider; the draw order decides whether the window sits under or over the rest of the interface. The settings panel shows a live preview of the window while you adjust it.
## Version: 1.3.0
## APIVersion: 101050 101051
## OptionalDependsOn: LibHarvensAddonSettings>=20106
## SavedVariables: PBsChatWindowCustomizer_Data

lang/strings.lua
lang/$(language).lua

Main.lua
Preview.lua
Settings.lua

